{
	"info": {
		"name": "18 · Images",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
		"description": "Generic image upload + serving (covers, avatars, icons) — the byte store behind evaluation covers, plus the public serve paths and the uploader-only delete.\n\n**Flow.** A) upload (⚠ manual file), fetch the bytes by key (public), mint a time-limited signed URL, fetch by that token; B) delete is **uploader-only** (a non-uploader is 403), the uploader deletes (204), fetch-after-delete is 404, an unauthenticated upload is 401, and a signed URL for an unknown key is 404.\n\n**⚠ Manual file (GUI-only run).** A Postman collection can't embed a binary, so the upload's `file` form-field has an empty `src` — in the Collection Runner / GUI, pick any JPEG/PNG/WebP. Because the downstream steps chain off the uploaded key, this collection is **run in the GUI** (the Collection Runner).\n\n**Auth model.** `{{admin_token}}` uploads/deletes; `{{viewer_token}}` probes the uploader-only 403; the serve paths (`GET /images/{key}`, `/signed`, `/signed-url`) are **public** (no auth) — the key/token is the capability. Self-contained — no `00-bootstrap`.\n\n**No dedicated permission** — images are non-sensitive; the boundary is *ownership* (delete) and *authentication* (upload), not a role.\n\n**Leftovers.** None — the asset is deleted in folder B.\n\n**Verified:** 13/13 checks green end-to-end against a live stack (`make up` + `make seedlocal`) — full flow run with a mounted file; the committed collection is GUI-run (the upload `file` `src` is empty for a manual pick)."
	},
	"auth": {
		"type": "noauth"
	},
	"variable": [
		{
			"key": "base_url",
			"value": "http://localhost:8000"
		},
		{
			"key": "run_suffix",
			"value": ""
		},
		{
			"key": "admin_token",
			"value": ""
		},
		{
			"key": "viewer_email",
			"value": "viewer@test.com"
		},
		{
			"key": "viewer_password",
			"value": "password123"
		},
		{
			"key": "viewer_token",
			"value": ""
		},
		{
			"key": "img_key",
			"value": ""
		},
		{
			"key": "img_token",
			"value": ""
		}
	],
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "Setup",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "1 · Log in as admin",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"auth": {
							"type": "noauth"
						},
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{admin_email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{admin_password}}\"\n}",
							"options": {
								"raw": {
									"language": "json"
								}
							}
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/auth/login",
							"host": [
								"{{base_url}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"v1",
								"auth",
								"login"
							]
						},
						"description": "Authenticate the seeded admin. Sets `run_suffix` (collision-free re-runs) and captures `admin_token`."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "prerequest",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.collectionVariables.set('run_suffix', Date.now().toString(36));"
								]
							}
						},
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('→ 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"pm.collectionVariables.set('admin_token', pm.response.json()['access_token']);"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "2 · Log in as viewer (non-admin)",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"auth": {
							"type": "noauth"
						},
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{viewer_email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{viewer_password}}\"\n}",
							"options": {
								"raw": {
									"language": "json"
								}
							}
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/auth/login",
							"host": [
								"{{base_url}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"v1",
								"auth",
								"login"
							]
						},
						"description": "Authenticate the seeded `viewer` (a non-admin identity) for the RBAC/isolation checks. Captures `viewer_token`."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('→ 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"pm.collectionVariables.set('viewer_token', pm.response.json()['access_token']);"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "A · Upload + serve",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "1 · Upload an image  ⚠ manual file",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [],
						"auth": {
							"type": "bearer",
							"bearer": [
								{
									"key": "token",
									"value": "{{admin_token}}"
								}
							]
						},
						"body": {
							"mode": "formdata",
							"formdata": [
								{
									"key": "file",
									"type": "file",
									"src": "",
									"description": "Pick any JPEG/PNG/WebP (<=20 MB)."
								}
							]
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/images",
							"host": [
								"{{base_url}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"v1",
								"images"
							]
						},
						"description": "**FE note:** any authenticated user uploads a cover/avatar/icon. **⚠ manual file:** in the GUI, select a JPEG/PNG/WebP for the `file` form-field (a collection can't embed a binary). The service sniffs the format with Pillow (not the Content-Type), caps at 20 MB, and downscales to <=1200x1200. Captures `img_key` (the opaque storage key)."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('→ 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
									"const d = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.collectionVariables.set('img_key', d.key);",
									"pm.test('returns key + url + dimensions', () => { pm.expect(d).to.have.property('key'); pm.expect(d).to.have.property('url'); pm.expect(d).to.have.property('width'); });"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "2 · Fetch by key (public)",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"auth": {
							"type": "noauth"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/images/{{img_key}}",
							"host": [
								"{{base_url}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"v1",
								"images",
								"{{img_key}}"
							]
						},
						"description": "The bytes are served **unauthenticated** — the UUID key is the capability — with a long-lived immutable `Cache-Control`."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('→ 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "3 · Mint a signed URL (public)",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"auth": {
							"type": "noauth"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/images/signed-url?key={{img_key}}",
							"host": [
								"{{base_url}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"v1",
								"images",
								"signed-url"
							],
							"query": [
								{
									"key": "key",
									"value": "{{img_key}}"
								}
							]
						},
						"description": "A time-limited `itsdangerous`-signed token wrapping the key + timestamp (TTL `MEDIA_SIGNED_URL_TTL_SECONDS`, ~15 min). Deliberately not S3-presigned, so it stays backend-agnostic. Captures `img_token`."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('→ 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"const d = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.test('url + expiry', () => { pm.expect(d).to.have.property('url'); pm.expect(d).to.have.property('expires_at'); });",
									"pm.collectionVariables.set('img_token', d.url.split('/').pop());"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "4 · Fetch via signed token (public)",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"auth": {
							"type": "noauth"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/images/signed/{{img_token}}",
							"host": [
								"{{base_url}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"v1",
								"images",
								"signed",
								"{{img_token}}"
							]
						},
						"description": "Streams the same bytes by token; the fetch path carries no key of its own. An expired/forged token is 403."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('→ 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "B · Delete + negatives",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "1 · Delete by a non-uploader → 403",
					"request": {
						"method": "DELETE",
						"header": [],
						"auth": {
							"type": "bearer",
							"bearer": [
								{
									"key": "token",
									"value": "{{viewer_token}}"
								}
							]
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/images/{{img_key}}",
							"host": [
								"{{base_url}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"v1",
								"images",
								"{{img_key}}"
							]
						},
						"description": "Delete is **uploader-only** — another authenticated user cannot remove someone else's asset."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('→ 403', () => pm.response.to.have.status(403));"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "2 · Delete by the uploader → 204",
					"request": {
						"method": "DELETE",
						"header": [],
						"auth": {
							"type": "bearer",
							"bearer": [
								{
									"key": "token",
									"value": "{{admin_token}}"
								}
							]
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/images/{{img_key}}",
							"host": [
								"{{base_url}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"v1",
								"images",
								"{{img_key}}"
							]
						},
						"description": "The uploader (admin) removes their own asset."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('→ 204', () => pm.response.to.have.status(204));"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "3 · Fetch after delete → 404",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"auth": {
							"type": "noauth"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/images/{{img_key}}",
							"host": [
								"{{base_url}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"v1",
								"images",
								"{{img_key}}"
							]
						},
						"description": "Confirms the delete."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('→ 404', () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "4 · Upload with no token → 401",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [],
						"auth": {
							"type": "noauth"
						},
						"body": {
							"mode": "formdata",
							"formdata": [
								{
									"key": "file",
									"type": "file",
									"src": "",
									"description": "Pick any JPEG/PNG/WebP (<=20 MB)."
								}
							]
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/images",
							"host": [
								"{{base_url}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"v1",
								"images"
							]
						},
						"description": "Upload requires authentication — the 401 fires before body validation, so this needs no file."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('→ 401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "5 · Signed URL for an unknown key → 404",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"auth": {
							"type": "noauth"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/images/signed-url?key=2026/01/01/deadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeef.png",
							"host": [
								"{{base_url}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"v1",
								"images",
								"signed-url"
							],
							"query": [
								{
									"key": "key",
									"value": "2026/01/01/deadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeef.png"
								}
							]
						},
						"description": "Minting a signed URL for a non-existent asset is a 404."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('→ 404', () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				}
			]
		}
	]
}
